    "result_text": "Owner responses now include `selfLink`, set to `/api/owners/` followed by the owner's id. The full test suite passes: 24 tests, no failures or errors, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink`.\n\nThe owner response model is generated from the API spec, so the change touches two places:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**: added `selfLink` to the `Owner` schema as a read-only string, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and the API docs describe it.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: added a `toSelfLink(owner)` method, used the same way as the existing `toInitials`. It returns `\"/api/owners/\" + id`, or nothing if the owner hasn't been saved yet.\n\nBecause the field is filled in when an owner is converted to a response, it appears everywhere owners are returned: create, get, list and the v2 paged list. The create response's `Location` header already used the same path, so the two now match.",
